# The list holds int32s by Link, and what it gives is cut to an int32. Whoever cuts takes the word as it lies in the list while it is no hole's. A number that is converted and held against itself to
# show that it is whole counts as an integer found too, and costs four to seven instructions more.
# The sizes are what the loops of f1 hold (the turns laid out, the written turn, the closed copy), and two more. While the number of the element was a join they held 27, 15 and 27:
